From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:08:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: duo: policy routing for Android containers

Waydroid runs Android in a container on the Surface Duo. Android's netd
keeps the routes of each network in a routing table of its own and
selects it with fwmark rules; without IP_MULTIPLE_TABLES every `ip rule`
call fails with EOPNOTSUPP and Android never gets a default route, so
apps see "Network is unreachable" although DHCP worked.

Enable policy routing for IPv4 and IPv6 and the mark/connmark/owner
matches netd uses.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the
direction of Bryson, who tested it on his Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/duo.config | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config b/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config
index e30896524..dc98a33a0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config
@@ -504,3 +504,12 @@ CONFIG_CRYPTO_XTS=y
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_ESSIV=y
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_HASH=y
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_SKCIPHER=y
+# Waydroid (Android apps on Debian, 2026-11-08): Android's netd puts every network's routes in its own table chosen by
+# fwmark rules - without policy routing `ip rule` fails ("Operation not supported") and Android has no default route
+CONFIG_IP_ADVANCED_ROUTER=y
+CONFIG_IP_MULTIPLE_TABLES=y
+CONFIG_IPV6_MULTIPLE_TABLES=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_MARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_MARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_CONNMARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_OWNER=y
